From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:47:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/43] Metal diamond engine: the grid as compile-time
 constants (snapshot cg26)

The kernel is compiled per model already (one macro per extension); the grid dimensions
now come in as preprocessor constants too, so the index arithmetic divides by constants
(z % nv and z / nv in every float index, i / nz in the Mur stages), and the Dims buffer
argument is gone. The Mur face and UPML box records are passed by value, so the stage
loops keep them in registers instead of loading them again after every store through a
device pointer that may alias the fields.

Paired interleaved A/B against cg25 (5 rounds, other processes on 4-5 cores): notch
tutorial x1.06 [1.03-1.18] (above cg24 again), SMA launch x1.03 [1.02-1.06], GCPW line
x1.02 [0.98-1.05], notch x3 x1.02, patch x5 x1.01.

emsKit diamond_check.sh 54 of 54. All six benchmark models bit-identical to the
multithreaded engine with OPENEMS_FTZ=1.

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
